  "security_implications": "The msg unpacker FIFO for share 0 processes potentially secret message data. ClearOnRead is enabled, requiring that the FIFO reliably zeroizes any read data to prevent leakage. Failure to thoroughly clear all storage bits (e.g., due to functional gating or resetless flops) could leave secret residues that persist across operations, leading to data exposure when the FIFO is later read or scanned. The unconnected depth_o output may prevent detection of overflow conditions that could corrupt or drop message data, though the impact may be limited to integrity rather than secrecy.",
